HST Office packaging: quote paths when creating the download tarball.

The installer names its output directories after PRODUCTNAME ("HST Office_26.8.1.1_Linux_x86-64_deb");
create_tar_gz_file_from_directory() passed them unquoted to the shell, so
the tar step failed on the space and the whole deb run was renamed
*_deb_witherror. Quoting the three paths is behaviour-neutral for names
without spaces.

License: modified upstream file keeps its license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/solenv/bin/modules/installer/download.pm
+++ b/solenv/bin/modules/installer/download.pm
@@ -509,7 +509,7 @@
         unlink("$installdir/install");
     }
 
-    my $systemcall = "cd $changedir; $fakerootstring tar -cf - $packdir | $installer::globals::packertool > $targzname";
+    my $systemcall = "cd \"$changedir\"; $fakerootstring tar -cf - \"$packdir\" | $installer::globals::packertool > \"$targzname\"";
 
     my $returnvalue = system($systemcall);
 
